        readonly 'community.merge.body.new': "Extract the archive's files into {newRoot}, keeping archive-relative paths. This workspace holds no research data yet, so there is nothing to back up.";
        readonly 'community.merge.action.merge': "Merge (same research)";
        readonly 'community.merge.body.merge': "For every category ④ file, read both sides first and produce **one merged file**:\n· Text / structured (.md/.tex/.json/.yaml/.csv…): information from **both** sides must survive. Not concatenation — merge by the file's semantics (research-state by dimension, plans by de-duplicating plan items, papers by section, evidence/claims/references as a de-duplicated union).\n· If the two sides state conclusions that cannot both hold: do not decide for me and do not drop either side — list the conflict in the report and keep both readings distinguishable, for me to adjudicate.\n· Binary / media (figures, PDFs, archives…): cannot be merged semantically — keep the newer mtime in place and **move** the other to {incoming}<original relative path> (do not delete), reporting both mtimes.\n· Machine-generated (caches / dependencies / build output / backups): skip, one line in the report.\nWrite category ① straight into {root}; leave category ② completely alone.";
        readonly 'community.merge.action.switch': "Back up the current research root, then extract a new one";
        readonly 'community.merge.body.switch': "1. **Back up** (move, never delete): move {backupFrom} into a backup directory **under this workspace root** (a sibling of the research work, not inside the root) — move rather than copy, so the new research root starts empty; the backup must stay in place and be recoverable.\n   {backupNameHint}\n   {layoutNote}\n2. **Extract**: write the archive's files, keeping relative paths, into {newRoot}.\n3. Do not modify or delete anything inside the backup directory.\n4. Report the **final name of the backup directory** (that is how I will find the old research again).";
        readonly 'community.merge.backupNote.nested': "(The research root is `<workspace>/workspace`; move that whole directory.)";
        readonly 'community.merge.backupNote.legacy': "(This is the **legacy layout**: research data sits directly in the workspace root. Move only the research files/directories into the backup; leave the user's own material — source papers, datasets, notes — untouched.)";
        readonly 'community.merge.action.decide': "Act on your judgement (same → merge; different → back up, then extract)";
        readonly 'community.merge.body.decide': "First state your judgement (same research / different research) and its basis in the report, **wait for my confirmation**, then act on the matching branch:\n· **Same** → merge: for every category ④ file, read both sides and produce a merged file that keeps information from both; list conflicts as they are instead of deciding. Write category ① into {root}; leave category ② alone.\n· **Different** → back up + extract: move {backupFrom} into a backup directory **under this workspace root** (move, not copy — recoverable; name it by the rule above and report the final name), then extract the archive into {newRoot} keeping relative paths.\nEither way, never delete content from either side.";
        readonly 'community.merge.zipPending': " (the name is the **pre-check guess**: if the file on disk ends with a suffix like `-2`, use that same-prefixed `.zip`; and **if it is still downloading, wait until it has fully landed before starting**.)";
        readonly 'community.merge.pendingHint': "Downloading: the merge prompt is **already filled into the input box** — send it once this download has landed (sending now would point at a half-written zip).";
        readonly 'community.merge.nameChanged': "The file actually written is `{name}` (different from the pre-check guess).";
        readonly 'community.merge.refill': "Update prompt with the real filename";
        readonly 'community.merge.downloadFailedHint': "Do **not** send the prompt already in the input box — the zip never landed.";
        readonly 'community.merge.identityWrite': "Finally write {identityFile} (the identity of this research: it is what lets the workspace identify itself after being copied or moved) and include its final content in the report:\n{identityJson}";
        readonly 'community.merge.identitySkip': "(The server provided no research identity — skip writing {identityFile}.)";
        readonly 'community.merge.prompt': "Integrate the research snapshot just downloaded from ConvFusion into this workspace — as a **merge / fresh extract / replacement**, never a blind overwrite.\n\nArchive: {zip}{zipNote}\nThis workspace: {workspace}\nIts current research root: {root}\n{plan}\n\n═══ Step 1: read-only survey (do NOT modify, create or delete any file) ═══\n\nCompare the archive's file list (relative path + size) against the files already in {root} and report four categories, item by item:\n  ① in the archive only (would be added)      — list all\n  ② local only (must be kept as-is)           — list all\n  ③ in both, identical content (nothing to do)— report the count\n  ④ in both, different content                — for each: path, both sizes and mtimes, type (text / structured / binary / machine-generated), and one line on how they differ\n\n**Stop after reporting and wait for my confirmation** — do not start step 2.\n\n═══ Step 2: {actionTitle} (after I confirm) ═══\n\n{actionBody}\n{identity}\n\n═══ Report ═══\n1. Per-file disposition: added n / merged m / identical-skipped k / local-only kept j / binary newer-wins b / backed up b / generated-skipped c\n2. For each merged or replaced file: one line on what was combined and which side's content survived\n3. Conflicts you could not adjudicate (if any)\n\nBoundary: only touch paths inside this workspace; do not delete the archive itself; touch nothing else.";
